# onnxruntime-gpu for the Jetson LocalServer images (JP5 / JP6 / JP7): the one
# place that names, per JetPack line, the ORT release the image carries, the
# exact upstream release commit its source build checks out, and the sha256 of
# the wheel that build produced.
#
# install_onnxruntime_gpu.sh reads this file in two places:
#   1. A wheel listed here that is staged beside the script in
#      onnxruntime-wheels/ (a gitignored directory build-custom.sh fills from the
#      account's component bucket, key onnxruntime-wheels/<file>) is installed
#      instead of compiling; it is used only when its sha256 equals the value
#      here, and both scripts stop on a mismatch (nothing unlisted is installed).
#   2. With no staged wheel the source build clones the onnxruntime repository
#      and checks out the release commit recorded here (a commit id, not a tag,
#      so the checkout does not depend on which tags a mirror carries) and stops
#      unless the tree's VERSION_NUMBER equals the version recorded here.
#
# Every wheel listed here was produced by install_onnxruntime_gpu.sh from the
# upstream release of its JetPack line and shipped in a published LocalServer
# image; the commit id is the one the wheel's own build info reports
# (onnxruntime.get_build_info(), git-commit-id). To add or replace an entry, see
# README.md "ONNX Runtime wheels for the Jetson images".
#
# Columns: <jetpack major> <ort version> <wheel file name> <sha256 of the wheel> <upstream release commit>
5 1.16.3 onnxruntime_gpu-1.16.3-cp311-cp311-linux_aarch64.whl 6c3379b996331ca5ca69327cbd18f3f44b8b4cb1ced2336453af4c4a48b7645a 2ac381c55397dffff327cc6efecf6f95a70f90a1
